.TH TICKER 1 "October 2026"
.SH NAME
ticker \- event-driven scrolling status ticker
.SH SYNOPSIS
ticker
.SH DESCRIPTION
ticker
reads newline-delimited events from standard input
and writes formatted messages to
/tmp/current-ticker.
.SH INPUT
Events may be supplied through a pipe, FIFO, or
directly from the terminal.
Each event must be terminated by a newline.
.PP
Each input line begins with an event prefix,
followed by the message text.
.TP
M:
Updates the persistent media message.
.TP
N:
Queues a temporary notification, which is displayed
twice before returning to the persistent message.
An audible alert is played using
paplay(1).
.PP
Unrecognised input is ignored.
Messages exceeding the display width scroll automatically.

.SH FILES
.TP
/tmp/current-ticker
Output file containing the current display text.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Requires
paplay(1)
for notification sounds.
.PP
Designed for use with
slstatus(1),
although any program capable of reading the output
file may consume its contents.
.PP
playerctl
and
tiramisu
are optional event sources.
